      "content": "Thanks for the start. It looks like you're getting a lot of the terms in there, but it's feeling a bit disconnected in the third paragraph—it's almost like you're just listing them in brackets. \n\nThe thing is, even though we need a high score to pass the filter, I can't send it to the client looking like a list of keywords. It has to actually sound like a professional engineering proposal that makes sense. If the human reviewers see it's just a word salad, they'll reject it immediately after the automated part.\n\nCan you try again? Try to weave the terms in more naturally so the technical arguments actually hold up, but please, keep that score high. We absolutely need to stay above that 0.8 threshold to survive the first round.",
